{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HARNESS RUN #1 FAILED ON THIS HOST — definitive, with the exact cause. Recording because it changes what this story can promise and where its acceptance evidence can come from.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED: the container ran ~25 minutes and then EXITED 1. It was NOT a config error and NOT a download failure. Jira really did come down and start booting — the log confirms 'JIRA Build : 8.17.1#817001-sha1:36e93c711dfb14e6e1509a2fef6b04c4d73cc7ca', Tomcat 8x started, H2 configured, plugin system starting. The fatal line is:\n  DeployerWatchdog: Deployable [http://localhost:2990/cargocpc/index.html] failed to finish deploying within the timeout period [600000]\n  ERROR Failed to execute goal com.atlassian.maven.plugins:jira-maven-plugin:8.0.2:run: Cannot start container [Tomcat8xInstalledLocalContainer]\nSo **Cargo's deploy watchdog has a hardcoded-by-default 600000 ms (10 minute) ceiling, and Jira cannot finish booting inside it under arm64 emulation.** The upstream README's '~3-5 minutes' is a native-amd64 figure; emulated, boot exceeds 10 minutes and Cargo kills it.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND THIS HOST: the 600s ceiling is a property of the harness, not of my laptop. Any slow or contended runner — an emulated arch, a throttled CI box, a cold Maven cache competing for I/O — hits the same wall. A readiness probe with a generous timeout does NOT help, because the container is dead before the probe could ever succeed: the failure is INSIDE the container's own startup, not in our polling. That is a distinction the plan had wrong by implication.\n\nMITIGATION UNDER TEST (not asserted): rebuilt with the entrypoint raised to\n  ENTRYPOINT [\"atlas-run\", \"-DskipAllPrompts=true\", \"-DstartupTimeout=2700000\", \"-Dcargo.timeout=2700000\"]\nand started it on :2991 with a PERSISTENT Maven volume (jira-m2-cache) so the ~917-artifact download is not repeated. Measuring now. I am deliberately not claiming the flags work until observed — the point of this story is a harness that provably starts, so an unverified flag would be exactly the kind of assumption the epic exists to eliminate.\n\nREGARDLESS OF THE OUTCOME, the plan must state: (a) the Cargo startup-timeout override belongs in the vendored Dockerfile with this failure recorded as the reason, or a maintainer will 'clean up' the flag and reintroduce a 25-minute silent death; (b) a native-amd64 runner is a REQUIREMENT for practical use, not a preference; and (c) acceptance evidence for this story must name the architecture it was produced on."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785362268158470001,"uuid":"a9637833-5aad-4f08-9c7a-a1b197962fd1"}